+ *                 NULL hard-IRQ handler, FALLING edge only - finalized from
+ *                 real TOUCH-D0-DIAG live evidence classifying GPIO79 as
+ *                 IDLE_HIGH_ACTIVE_LOW (zero invariant violations across 78
+ *                 real touch events, two boots - see
+ *                 docs/NEBULAOS_TOUCH_IRQ_TRIGGER_FINDINGS.md). Zero I2C
+ *                 transfers, zero coordinate/input processing in the
+ *                 handler - the existing 30ms poll keeps running completely
+ *                 unchanged and unconditionally in this mode too.
+ *   irq-assist  - only reachable after irq-observe has been selected at
+ *                 least once this boot. Idle state arms the falling-edge
+ *                 IRQ plus a conservative 250ms safety poll as a fallback
+ *                 net. On the IRQ firing: mask the line (so a held touch
+ *                 can't keep re-firing) and switch the *existing* poll
+ *                 cadence to the normal 30ms rate for the duration of the
+ *                 contact - all I2C/coordinate work happens in that
+ *                 existing poll/report path, never reimplemented and never
+ *                 done from IRQ context. On release (detected by the
+ *                 existing release logic, unchanged), confirm GPIO79 reads
+ *                 idle-high, drop back to the 250ms safety poll, re-arm the
+ *                 IRQ.
+ *
+ * Fail-safe: an IRQ request failure, an IRQ storm (>50 events in a rolling
+ * 1-second window), a repeated IRQ during one already-held irq-assist
+ * contact, a failed release confirmation, an inconsistent pen state
+ * transition, or a failed internal mode-transition action all permanently
+ * fall the device back to poll-only for the remainder of that boot -
+ * exactly one ratelimited kernel warning, never per-event log spam. This is
+ * a one-way trip: once tripped, only "poll-only" can ever be selected again
+ * until reboot.
+ */
+#define NS2009_QUAL_STORM_WINDOW_MS		1000
+#define NS2009_QUAL_STORM_THRESHOLD		50
+#define NS2009_QUAL_SAFETY_POLL_INTERVAL_MS	250
